       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. That's twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg per day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day in total.** For example, 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO two or three times daily.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intended, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
