       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 1,700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. No indication I know of supports it, and for this patient (70 kg, normal kidney and liver function) it would mainly add risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or any other dose up to the maximum.\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you have a clinical reason for going above the maximum, a pharmacist can review it with you and document it.\n- **Enter it yourself.** You can place the order directly in the order-entry system, where it will go through the hospital's own dose-check and override process.\n\nIf 1,700 mg was meant as a total daily dose or the number came from a transcription error, tell me the intended regimen and I'll enter it."
      }
